James inquired about sharing code between a Shiny app and an analysis project located in separate directories. I recommended creating a shared directory accessible by both projects and sourcing the shared code from there. James then asked whether the shared code would also be deployed when pushing the app online. I clarified that shared code should be included in the app's directory to ensure visibility upon deployment. He further confirmed this approach as sensible. When he asked about uploading a common library directory with his deployment code, I suggested modifying the `deployApp` function to include the shared code in the deployment process. I provided a structured solution, emphasizing the importance of testing after deployment to ensure functionality.
